1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Hi, I'm Emmanuel, and this is SafeSpace —

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
a trusted rights-information and protection platform
for young people in Kenya.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Young people facing sensitive situations
don't just need information.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
They need information they can understand,
verify, and safely act on.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
SafeSpace is built around four principles:
Understand, Verify, Act and Protect.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Unlike a conventional AI chatbot, SafeSpace does not
treat AI as the source of legal truth.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Verified evidence is retrieved first, and AI only
helps explain that evidence.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Here, a young person asks whether pregnancy means
they can be sent away from school.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
SafeSpace identifies the relevant journey and retrieves
verified information from its curated Kenyan knowledge base.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
It provides a plain-language explanation together with
its source and appropriate next steps.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The user can see not only the answer, but exactly where
that information came from and when it was last verified.

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Sensitive safety questions are handled differently.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Before any AI generation, SafeSpace runs deterministic
safety classification based on verified rules.

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
When elevated risk is detected, safety and appropriate
support pathways become prominent.

15
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The AI cannot downgrade this deterministic
safety classification.

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
But information you can trust also means knowing
when NOT to answer.

17
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Tax law is outside SafeSpace's verified knowledge base.

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Instead of asking AI to guess, SafeSpace returns
an insufficient evidence response —

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:20,000
and does not call AI at all.

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:28,000
SafeSpace would rather say it does not have enough
verified information than provide an unsupported answer.

21
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:35,000
No account is required to use SafeSpace.
Questions are not intentionally persisted by the platform.

22
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Quick Exit allows a user to leave the application immediately.

23
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:50,000
The MVP uses Django, PostgreSQL, Next.js and TypeScript,
with controlled OpenAI integration.

24
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:58,000
The architecture creates a path toward locally verified
knowledge packs for other jurisdictions.

25
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:05,000
SafeSpace demonstrates a different approach to AI
for sensitive public information.

26
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,000
We don't ask AI what your rights are.
We find verified rights information first.

27
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:15,000
That's SafeSpace: information you can understand,
verify, act on — and trust.
